Subject: Synchronize renderer options before applying an ICC profile
Origin: ChengYingPlayer maintainers
Modified-Date: 2026-09-17
Applied-to: mpv 0.38.0 after the upstream ICC ownership backport

The public render API may follow a synchronous icc-profile-auto option change
before another frame has refreshed the renderer's option cache. Refresh on the
render thread before checking that option, using the same function already
called at the beginning of frame rendering. This keeps disabled-auto behavior
unchanged and avoids silently discarding a newly enabled display profile.

--- a/video/out/gpu/video.c
+++ b/video/out/gpu/video.c
@@ -607,6 +607,7 @@ bool gl_video_gamma_auto_enabled(struct gl_video *p)
 //          takes over ownership.
 void gl_video_set_icc_profile(struct gl_video *p, bstr icc_data)
 {
+    gl_video_update_options(p);
     if (gl_lcms_set_memory_profile(p->cms, icc_data))
         reinit_from_options(p);
 }
